WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Between classes and assignments, an urge can feel as if it must be followed now.
But urgency is not a command.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Pause. Breathe in for four counts, hold for two, and breathe out for six.
A short pause creates room to choose an action aligned with your goal.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Name today's goal. Close the access, switch to a safe activity,
or contact someone you trust. You do not have to face the urge alone.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Gamblock-AI is designed as a student support tool: local detection,
a Pattern Interrupt, consent-based accountability, and web self-regulation.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:15.000
On supported browsers, URL rules and bounded title, heading, and anchor text
are processed with Bag-of-Words and Logistic Regression.
The decision stays on the device.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:31.000
URLs, domains, DOM content, history, screenshots, and page scores are not sent to the server.
Account and voluntary recovery features have separate purposes and controls.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:47.000
When an indication is detected, the native app blocks and shows a seven-second visual pause.
The user can then choose grounding or web recovery without sending the page address.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:02:04.000
An accountability partner is a parent or peer selected through consent.
They can help review removal requests, but cannot see history,
journals, mood, or private recovery detail.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:20.000
The web journey supports intentions, check-ins, impulse education, small missions,
cross-program skills, and reflection on the next adjustment.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:35.000
Gamblock-AI is currently a code-complete prototype.
Model, device, resilience, retention, and psychological-outcome evaluation
still requires execution and review.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:45.000
Start with one pause and one safer choice.
Open Gamblock-AI to learn, arrange support, or find help.
